==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|enm|en}}, from {{etyl|la|en}} {{m|la|gibbus||humped, hunched}}, probably cognate with {{m|la|cubō||bend oneself, lie down}}, Italian {{m|it|gobba||humpback}}, Greek {{m|el|κύφος||humpback, bent}}, {{m|el|κύβος||cube, vertebra}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈɡɪbəs/|lang=en}}
* {{rhymes|ɪbəs|lang=en}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# Characterized by [[convex|convexity]]; [[protuberant]].
#* '''1886''', Thomas Hardy, ''The Mayor of Casterbridge'', [[s:The Mayor of Casterbridge/Chapter 22|chapter 22]]
#*: In fact, what these '''gibbous''' human shapes specially represented was ready money—money insistently ready [...]
# {{lb|en|astronomy}} Phase of [[moon]] or [[planet]] between first quarter and full or between full and last [[quarter]].
# [[humpback|Humpbacked]].
#* '''1697''', Dryden, ''Aeneid'', [[s:Aeneid (Dryden)/Book VIII|book 8]]
#*: A pointed flinty rock, all bare and black,
#*: Grew '''gibbous''' from behind the mountain's back;

